# Architecture Overview (High-level)

This document replaces per-module rules for the crawler with a high-level project structure view. Module-specific rules may be reintroduced later when needed.

## Layers & Key Modules

- App/API

  - [src/app/main.py](mdc:src/app/main.py): FastAPI app, lifespan loads config and emits startup banner.
  - [src/app/cli.py](mdc:src/app/cli.py): `dev`/`prod` wrappers for `fastapi dev/run` with `APP_ENV`.

- Configuration

  - [src/app/config.py](mdc:src/app/config.py): dotenv + Hydra composition, exposes `cfg`.
  - [src/conf/config.yaml](mdc:src/conf/config.yaml), env: [dev.yaml](mdc:src/conf/env/dev.yaml), [prod.yaml](mdc:src/conf/env/prod.yaml).

- Core (Domain)

  - File Crawler: [src/core/file_crawler/extractor.py](mdc:src/core/file_crawler/extractor.py), [models.py](mdc:src/core/file_crawler/models.py).
  - AI (planned): embeddings, LLM orchestration, chunking using LangChain.
  - Services (planned): indexing/search orchestration, pipelines.

- Infra (planned)

  - DB repositories, storage adapters, external services.

- Utils
  - [src/utils/paths.py](mdc:src/utils/paths.py): project root/source detection, path helpers.

## Data Flow (planned end-to-end)

1. Root selection → file traversal (crawler) → metadata extraction.
2. Text extraction/chunking (AI pipeline) → embedding batches.
3. Vector store write (Qdrant) + metadata/payload indexing (SQLite planned for meta store).
4. Query handling: NL → structured filters → multi-query embeddings → vector search (+filters) → result post-processing.

## Cross-cutting Policies

- Configuration-first: all environment-dependent behavior comes from Hydra config.
- Logging: no secrets in logs; banner shows only non-sensitive metadata.
- Error handling: crawler skips permission/missing entries; pipelines prefer fail-soft per item.

## Future Rule Split (when needed)

- Introduce module-specific rules for: Embeddings, Qdrant, SQLite meta store, pipelines, and CLI contracts when components stabilize.
